---
description: Readable serif is sized against the surrounding sans
globs: "**/*.{vue,scss}"
alwaysApply: true
---

Body text and UI chrome stay sans.

When serif is used for readable text — stems, choice labels, record lines, text-like buttons — set its size to 1.2 × the surrounding sans size, and never below `1rem`. Headings may be larger serif; the floor still applies.

Example: a radio label beside 1rem sans chrome is `font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.2rem;`.
